{"id": "1545668912744628255", "channel_id": "1545385622317965442", "author_id": "337701342900387851", "author_name": "purpleater", "content": "Many of the adjustments we've seen recently (affinity, scrip store, d-tide) should have been run through player-led testers first. I doubt that finding willing volunteers for this kind of stuff should be an issue. \n\nI'll take the 100 pulls but it doesn't reflect well given the execution of the issue and the responses that have followed. The community has made it obvious that future developments pertaining to these issues will be observed intensely and scrutinized even more so. Taking the time to slow down and actually understand/navigate players' complaints will reflect better than a metric fuck-ton of pulls anyways.", "timestamp": "2026-09-05T05:36:25.938000+00:00", "thread_id": "1545385622317965442", "edited_timestamp": "2026-09-05T05:37:01.185000+00:00", "reactions": [{"emoji": "Celeste_agree", "emoji_id": "1400771815076528258", "count": 11}], "thread_title": "On the D-Effect Zone Adjustments", "forum_channel_id": "1184003940082262069"}
